# Level 2's own objects as the original runs them: level 1 won at its 20th
# frame ($A07 and $A6C set, as its boss's payout does), so the game loads
# level 2 as it would (only level 1 is kept in memory; the others' sectors
# are known once the one before is loaded); the ship kept alive, still and
# firing, the shop skipped (as level-run.exp); at frame 6700 (the world held
# at 2528 by the mid boss, $CE8) the mid boss taken as destroyed ($CE8
# cleared, $DA6 set, as $50C3E does) so the world goes on. Logged every frame ($3E42): the frame, the world line,
# fire, the ship and the random generator; every scenery and wave record
# fired (the level's handlers $4FD64, $4FF8C); every enemy destroyed
# ($6250); every update of an object of the level's own code as it starts
# (the wall gun $4FAE2, the burst block $4F88E, the crawler $4FC06, the
# eggs $4F710 and $4F540, the hatchlings $50346, the spores $50798, the
# hole creatures $508D0, the mid boss's parts $50C48, the end boss $50DE6):
# its pc, object, type, x, y, +40, +48 and hit points. For porting level
# 2's own code frame by frame.
# Run with --trace fdc.
expect prompt read sector sector=0x1 .*tr=0x0 .*addr=0x6760e
stage level2-jump.ini
stage level2-past.ini
stage level2-objs-start.ini
stage weapons-frame.ini
stage waves-scen.ini
stage waves-wave.ini
stage waves-kill.ini
stage level2-obj.ini
stage level-run-shield.ini
stage level-run-nodeath.ini
stage level-run-nowall.ini
stage level-run-noshop.ini
# Hatari 2.6 loses its breakpoints when a hit adds the 16th (it grows the
# array without copying it): grow it here, outside any hit, then clear it.
debug b pc = $1
debug b pc = $2
debug b pc = $3
debug b pc = $4
debug b pc = $5
debug b pc = $6
debug b pc = $7
debug b pc = $8
debug b pc = $9
debug b pc = $a
debug b pc = $b
debug b pc = $c
debug b pc = $d
debug b pc = $e
debug b pc = $f
debug b pc = $10
debug b pc = $11
debug b pc = $12
debug b pc = $13
debug b pc = $14
debug b pc = $15
debug b pc = $16
debug b all
debug b pc = $7a50 :once :trace :file {run}/level2-objs-start.ini
disk-a {disk2}
sleep 8
fire
sleep 4
fire
expect level1-read read sector sector=0x3 .*tr=0xc .*addr=0x3e
quiet level1-loaded 3
fire
sleep 2
fire
sleep 2
